262
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:28,460
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Se Chan and Kyeong Hwan gets ready to prepare the chicken.)</font>

263
00:06:26,210 --> 00:06:27,880
<font size="64">- It's all here. - Do we have raw chicken?</font>

264
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,680
<font size="64">- It's here. - Gosh, look at this.</font>

265
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:30,990
<font size="64">What? The chicken is...</font>

266
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:32,360
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Unprepared raw chicken)</font>

267
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:32,490
<font size="64">We need to debone this.</font>

268
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:33,750
<font size="64">- We can just... - It's okay.</font>

269
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:34,960
<font size="64">- I can do this. - We should chop it.</font>

270
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:36,460
<font size="64">- Let's fry it whole. - We can fry it whole like before.</font>

271
00:06:34,970 --> 00:06:38,100
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Chef Yang is a reliable fried chicken veteran.)</font>

272
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:38,290
<font size="64">Let's cut it after frying it whole.</font>

273
00:06:38,490 --> 00:06:40,390
<font size="64">- Kyeong Hwan. - Yes.</font>

274
00:06:40,390 --> 00:06:41,860
<font size="64">Make sure to do well this time.</font>

275
00:06:41,860 --> 00:06:42,930
<font size="64">All right.</font>

276
00:06:42,210 --> 00:06:45,240
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(On the other hand, Chef Heo is not so reliable.)</font>

277
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:45,900
<font size="64">- It will be insane. - Last time, your dish...</font>

278
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:47,570
<font size="64">- Kyeong Hwan, your dish was... - It's here.</font>

279
00:06:47,670 --> 00:06:49,070
<font size="64">- Why... - Okay?</font>

280
00:06:49,070 --> 00:06:50,640
<font size="64">Why do you remember food for so long?</font>

281
00:06:50,640 --> 00:06:52,910
<font size="64">- Was that braised tuna? - It was last summer.</font>

282
00:06:51,280 --> 00:06:53,120
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Correct)</font>

283
00:06:52,910 --> 00:06:54,410
<font size="64">That was so bad. It was too bland.</font>

284
00:06:53,250 --> 00:06:56,350
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(It was a taste that even Seok Sam, who forgets everything, remembers.)</font>

285
00:06:54,410 --> 00:06:56,480
<font size="64">It tasted horrible.</font>

286
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,650
<font size="64">It was unbelievably bland.</font>

287
00:06:57,650 --> 00:07:00,210
<font size="64">Thank you for remembering my food.</font>

288
00:07:00,310 --> 00:07:01,720
<font size="64">First, this chicken...</font>

289
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:03,630
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(He has to succeed this time.)</font>

290
00:07:01,750 --> 00:07:03,180
<font size="64">Put it here.</font>

291
00:07:03,180 --> 00:07:04,420
<font size="64">Will you chop up the chicken here?</font>

292
00:07:04,420 --> 00:07:06,650
<font size="64">- No, I'm not chopping it up. - Okay.</font>

293
00:07:07,220 --> 00:07:09,120
<font size="64">- Are you frying the chicken whole? - Fry the chicken whole?</font>

294
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:11,460
<font size="64">We should have at least one whole fried chicken, though.</font>

295
00:07:11,730 --> 00:07:13,830
<font size="64">Do you want me to chop up the chicken and fry it, or...</font>

296
00:07:13,830 --> 00:07:15,430
<font size="64">- Chop it up first. - Should we cut it after frying?</font>

297
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,600
<font size="64">We have to cut it and then fry it.</font>

