00:07:16,170 --> 00:07:19,040
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(No way.)</font>

299
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,800
<font size="64">- That would be better. - To cook it all the way through.</font>

300
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,600
<font size="64">But it'd be nice to have a whole chicken, too.</font>

301
00:07:19,910 --> 00:07:22,380
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(A sudden heated debate over fried chicken)</font>

302
00:07:20,670 --> 00:07:21,670
<font size="64">Then...</font>

303
00:07:21,670 --> 00:07:23,270
<font size="64">- Just two... - Wait.</font>

304
00:07:23,270 --> 00:07:26,340
<font size="64">You can't fry it whole for yangnyeom fried chicken.</font>

305
00:07:26,340 --> 00:07:28,140
<font size="64">- We have to cut it first. - No.</font>

306
00:07:26,450 --> 00:07:29,550
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Cut after frying it whole versus cut and then fry it)</font>

307
00:07:28,140 --> 00:07:29,580
<font size="64">I know we should cut it for yangnyeom fried chicken.</font>

308
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:31,450
<font size="64">I'll look up how to do it.</font>

309
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,490
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Searching on YouTube right away)</font>

310
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:33,450
<font size="64">Why cut it?</font>

311
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,620
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Yangnyeom Chicken Recipe: Trim the wings, tail, and innards,)</font>

312
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,720
<font size="64">Cut off the tips of the wings.</font>

313
00:07:33,620 --> 00:07:34,730
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(and then cut into serving-sized pieces.)</font>

314
00:07:34,730 --> 00:07:37,060
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Normally, you're supposed to cut it.)</font>

315
00:07:36,050 --> 00:07:37,350
<font size="64">Trim the tail.</font>

316
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,550
<font size="64">What are you doing, Kyeong Hwan?</font>

317
00:07:38,550 --> 00:07:39,950
<font size="64">I need to check how to cut a chicken.</font>

318
00:07:39,950 --> 00:07:41,760
<font size="64">- What? - Are you using a whole chicken?</font>

319
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:42,790
<font size="64">Yes, a whole chicken.</font>

320
00:07:43,020 --> 00:07:44,760
<font size="64">I'm going to use uncut chicken.</font>

321
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:46,400
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Firm)</font>

322
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:48,100
<font size="64">- Uncut chicken? - Don't rely on YouTube too much.</font>

323
00:07:48,730 --> 00:07:50,500
<font size="64">Let's make our own dish.</font>

324
00:07:51,430 --> 00:07:52,570
<font size="64">But I don't think it will taste good.</font>

325
00:07:51,480 --> 00:07:53,410
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Unsure)</font>

326
00:07:52,570 --> 00:07:53,970
<font size="64">Let's go with our gut feeling.</font>

327
00:07:53,480 --> 00:07:56,480
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(They can't seem to agree.)</font>

328
00:07:53,970 --> 00:07:54,970
<font size="64">- Sure. - Are you sure?</font>

329
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:56,370
<font size="64">Kyeong Hwan is sneaking peeks at YouTube.</font>

330
00:07:56,370 --> 00:07:57,770
<font size="64">I should check it.</font>

331
00:07:57,810 --> 00:08:00,570
<font size="64">Are you going to fry it whole and then season it?</font>

332
00:08:00,570 --> 00:08:02,140
<font size="64">I'll fry the chicken whole...</font>

333
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:04,280
<font size="64">and then pour a sauce over it...</font>

334
00:08:04,280 --> 00:08:06,150
<font size="64">as a performance.</font>

335
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:08,830
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Chef Yang's recipe: Frying the chicken whole...)</font>

336
00:08:07,150 --> 00:08:08,480
<font size="64">Why cut it?</font>

337
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:10,620
<font size="64">I should check it.</font>

338
00:08:08,830 --> 00:08:10,800
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(and then pouring a sauce shower over it)</font>

339
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:13,050
<font size="64">- Please. - Look at him acting like a chef.</font>

340
00:08:13,050 --> 00:08:14,790
<font size="64">- Kyeong Hwan, just the tail... - You eat your chicken.</font>

341
00:08:14,790 --> 00:08:16,060
<font size="64">I'll eat mine.</font>

342
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:17,530
<font size="64">Are you frying it whole?</font>

343
00:08:16,530 --> 00:08:19,670
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Chef Heo's recipe: The traditional method of cutting it into pieces)</font>

344
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:19,730
<font size="64">You can't fry it whole for yangnyeom fried chicken.</font>

345
00:08:19,770 --> 00:08:22,610
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Chef Yang of Performance versus Chef Heo of Traditional Method)</font>

346
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:22,860
<font size="64">- I'm going to use uncut chicken. - We can't mess up the chicken.</font>

347
00:08:23,110 --> 00:08:26,540
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(In the end, the 2 chefs are prepping 1 chicken each.)</font>

348
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:28,950
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(After splitting it open...)</font>

349
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:29,200
<font size="64">I can cut it like this.</font>

350
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:30,820
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Wide open)</font>

351
00:08:31,340 --> 00:08:32,440
<font size="64">Onion?</font>

352
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:36,690
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Chef Yang cleans out the innards while leaving the chicken intact.)</font>

353
00:08:37,050 --> 00:08:38,720
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Meanwhile, Chef Heo...)</font>

354
00:08:37,140 --> 00:08:38,150
<font size="64">My goodness.</font>

355
00:08:42,820 --> 00:08:44,820
<font size="64">Chicken needs to be neat and easy to eat.</font>

356
00:08:43,290 --> 00:08:45,600
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(cuts it up into easy-to-eat pieces.)</font>

357
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:45,820
<font size="64">It's done.</font>

358
00:08:47,030 --> 00:08:49,900
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(While they prepare the chicken in their own different ways...)</font>

359
00:08:47,050 --> 00:08:48,390
<font size="64">- This is good. - All right.</font>

360
00:08:48,390 --> 00:08:49,920
<font size="64">Tell me if you need any help.</font>

361
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:51,060
<font size="64">No, we don't.</font>

362
00:08:51,160 --> 00:08:53,190
<font size="64">First, I'll make the sauce.</font>

363
00:08:52,100 --> 00:08:54,940
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Haha, in charge of budaejjigae, prepares the broth and seasoning.)</font>

364
00:08:57,340 --> 00:08:59,640
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Gochujang as the base of the broth)</font>

365
00:09:00,170 --> 00:09:01,340
<font size="64">And...</font>

366
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,970
<font size="64">dark soy sauce.</font>

367
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:04,270
<font size="64">Tuna sauce.</font>

368
00:09:05,650 --> 00:09:07,290
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(A handful of minced garlic)</font>

369
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:07,170
<font size="64">Is this too much?</font>

370
00:09:07,290 --> 00:09:08,520
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Winging it without any measurements)</font>

371
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:12,450
<font size="64">I kept thinking about that spicy fish stew ramyeon...</font>

372
00:09:12,450 --> 00:09:14,480
<font size="64">we couldn't eat during the day,</font>

373
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:16,380
<font size="64">- Wait, Haha. - and we're eating budaejjigae.</font>

374
00:09:16,380 --> 00:09:17,550
<font size="64">- Haha. - Yes?</font>

375
00:09:17,550 --> 00:09:19,590
<font size="64">You shouldn't make the budaejjigae thick and heavy.</font>

376
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:20,960
<font size="64">Thick and heavy?</font>

377
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,690
<font size="64">- It should be delicious. - I want it to be spicy.</font>

378
00:09:21,430 --> 00:09:23,300
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(A picky customer's request)</font>

379
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:26,970
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Adding chili powder for a spicy kick)</font>

380
00:09:28,540 --> 00:09:30,510
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(One more time)</font>

381
00:09:30,030 --> 00:09:31,770
<font size="64">I put in a lot of chili powder.</font>

382
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:33,600
<font size="64">You need a lot of chili powder.</font>

383
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,580
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(What does the seasoning taste like, thrown together by intuition?)</font>

384
00:09:36,410 --> 00:09:37,920
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Licking)</font>

385
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:40,880
<font size="64">Hey, Sauce Master.</font>

386
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:43,090
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(Getting confirmation from the head chef)</font>

387
00:09:43,140 --> 00:09:44,880
<font size="64">- Salty? - I thought you said Soju Master.</font>

388
00:09:46,550 --> 00:09:48,280
<font size="64">- I like it. - Good? It's not too salty, right?</font>

389
00:09:47,930 --> 00:09:50,590
<font size="64" color="#ffffcc">(He got an immediate okay.)</font>

390
00:09:48,280 --> 00:09:50,050
<font size="64">It should be at least this salty.</font>

391
00:09:50,050 --> 00:09:52,120
<font size="64">I like that there's no sweetness. It's perfect.</font>

392
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,260
<font size="64">- You can add onions for sweetness. - Okay.</font>

393
